00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.080
The map you see is a map of the whereabouts of the ten largest

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:07.040
gold mining companies in the world till the year 2020.

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:09.640
This map was revealed in March 2021

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:12.840
by the Canadian data company ‘Mining Intelligence’.

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:15.240
Now, I want you to be all ears to what is coming..

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:20.120
First thing to be noted is that; these ten big companies together

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:24.080
produced about 780 tons of gold in 2020,

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:26.840
which is worth about $48 billion.

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:30.280
This means that they together account for 22%

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:33.200
of the total global production of gold in the same year.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:37.600
Second thing to be noted is that; 3 of these companies are operating in Russia,

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:41.320
which is why Russia is considered one of the largest gold producers in the world.

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:44.400
Our main focus here is on the three large companies operating in Russia,

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:50.720
chief among which is the Russian gold giant Polyus;

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:54.440
the second is the Canadian Kinross Gold which major

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:57.440
production comes from Russia despite being Canadian as it

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:02.360
controls one of the largest Russian gold mines. this will not continue,

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:06.680
on April 5, it vocalled about selling its Russian assets to the

00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:12.080
Russian gold giant Highland Gold for $680 million due to the difficulties

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:16.600
it is experiencing in exploring because of the Western sanctions on Russia

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:19.520
then comes the third company which is Russia's Polymetal.

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:22.800
Russia has one of the largest gold reserves in the world

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:26.680
with estimated reserves of 5,500 tons.

00:01:26.680 --> 00:01:31.520
In 2021, it was the third largest gold producing country in the world

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:34.800
with approximately 310 tons of gold.

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:37.680
More than two-thirds of the Russian production comes from

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:41.360
the largest eight Russian gold mining companies that control

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:45.400
the largest gold mines in the country, led of course by the giant Polyus,

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:49.120
which alone produces more than 26% of the total

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:54.400
amount there, and then comes Polymetal.

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:57.760
Let's take a look at the 6 largest gold mines in Russia,

00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:00.640
their locations and quantities of gold.

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:04.160
By the way, five of them are controlled by Polyus.

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:09.200
The largest mine is Olimpiada, located in the Krasnoyarsk region in eastern Siberia.

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:15.280
It is the largest gold mine in Russia and the third largest gold mine in the world; owned and operated by Polyus.

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:19.600
The second mine, Kupol, is located in the Chukotka region in the

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:23.240
far east of Russia and is currently managed by the Canadian company Kinross Gold,

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:28.480
and its operating costs are among the lowest among the mines operated by the company over the globe.

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:32.880
The remaining four mines are all under polyus control, starting

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:37.640
with Russia's third largest, Blagodatnoye, located just 25

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:40.000
kilometers from the Olimpiada mine.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:44.240
Then Natalka, located in one of the coldest and most remote areas

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:48.080
in the north of the Russian Pacific coast in the Magadan Region,

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:53.120
was acquired by Polyus in 2008. Then comes Verninskoye which

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:59.560
is located in Bodaybo, a historical gold-mining city in the Irkutsk Oblast in Southeast Siberia.

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:02.160
Last but not least comes the sixth mine which is the Sukhoi Log,

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:06.200
one of the largest untapped gold deposits in the world and one

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:08.720
of the most important projects of the Russian gold giant Polyus.

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:13.040
The mine is a valley, its name means the Dry Valley.

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:17.680
It covers 105 thousand square kilometers in the Russian Irkutsk region.

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:22.400
It has reserves of 2,000 tons, which is an enormous amount of gold,

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:25.800
and its life span extends to 35 years.

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:29.960
The mine is still fully operational in 2026 and it is expected

00:03:29.960 --> 00:03:34.640
that Polyus will produce about 50 tons out of it annually, thus it

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:38.640
will be the second largest open-ended gold mine in the world

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:42.120
in terms of production after the giant Muruntau mine in Uzbekistan.

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:47.120
Obviously, gold is one of the most important natural resources owned by Russia.

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:54.120
That is why it is an important and significant piece of chess in the ongoing conflict between Russia and the West.

00:03:54.120 --> 00:04:00.400
After the Russian army entered the Ukraine, Western countries imposed all forms and types of

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:05.120
sanctions that can be imposed on the Russian economy, as all of you know.

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:07.200
Some important questions must be asked here:

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:10.240
Did Russia really peg its local currency, the ruble, to gold?

00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:13.080
Why did it do that? What is the effect of such a step? What does

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:16.680
it mean that the Western countries have banned dealing in Russian gold to the extent that there

00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:20.720
are companies that have hundreds of tons of gold without a way to unseat them?

