00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:10.760
In April 1999, Switzerland abolished the de facto gold standard

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:15.520
that had supported its local currency in accordance with the constitution.

00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:18.080
The Swiss franc has been linked to the euro ever since. Thus,

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:23.080
Switzerland was at that time the last country in the world to abolish the gold requirement to support the country's currency.

00:05:23.080 --> 00:05:27.160
However, on March 25, the Central Bank of Russia announced

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:32.960
that between March 28 and June 30 it will be buying gold at a fixed price

00:05:32.960 --> 00:05:39.800
of 5,000 rubles per gram, which is almost equal to $52

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:42.200
according to the exchange rate between the dollar and the ruble.

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:48.880
On the 7th of this month, it stated that it would continue to buy gold in rubles, but at a negotiated price; not fixed.

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:53.040
Definitely, the ruble rose in value against the dollar as a result.

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:57.960
At the day of this announcement, on March 25, a dollar was worth 102 rubles,

00:05:57.960 --> 00:06:03.080
currently at the time of writing the episode, on April 15, one dollar is worth 80 rubles.

00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:09.600
Thus, the ruble went back to its value before the Russo-Ukrainian war that broke out on February 24.

00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:13.960
Buying gold in rubles is an extension of a series of measures

00:06:13.960 --> 00:06:17.120
taken by the Russian Central Bank to support the ruble and

00:06:17.120 --> 00:06:24.000
prevent its devaluation. This decision comes immediately after the 'buy Russian gas in rubles' announcement on March 23.

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:28.360
It seems that this will not be the last Russian commodity to be circulated in ruble.

00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:36.000
We might be witnessing Russia selling oil, wheat, aluminum and other commodities that it exports in rubles, in the coming days. 

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:38.800
The underlying mechanism here is to circulate commodities in ruble

00:06:38.800 --> 00:06:42.680
Russia gives further more value to its currency globally

00:06:42.680 --> 00:06:46.080
through creating a demand to ruble in the exchange market all over the world.

00:06:46.080 --> 00:06:50.280
This goes, of course, in line with its attempts over the years, together with China,

00:06:50.280 --> 00:06:53.440
to weaken the dominance of the US dollar on the global economy,

00:06:53.440 --> 00:06:57.960
one of the reasons for which is that most international commodities are priced in dollars.

00:06:57.960 --> 00:07:05.760
Let's focus on buying gold specifically in rubles. As noticed, Russia has set a time period for buying gold in rubles,

00:07:05.760 --> 00:07:10.920
lasting only to the end of the next June, after which we do not know whether it will be renewed or not.

00:07:10.920 --> 00:07:15.880
What I want to say is that such a step, although it greatly supported the ruble,

00:07:15.880 --> 00:07:20.520
if not implemented well, will turn against Russia. Therefore, setting the time

00:07:20.520 --> 00:07:25.560
period for the purchase of gold in rubles by the Central Bank of Russia was a smart move.

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:30.280
Why is it dangerous and may turn against Russia making the ruble lose its value?

00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:34.680
Let us first and quickly explain the Bretton Woods system, how did it go!

00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:42.360
After WWII, in the year 1944, all the major countries in the world were suffering the losses of the First and Second World Wars,

00:07:42.360 --> 00:07:47.360
except for the United States as it controlled two-thirds of the world’s gold at the time

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:50.840
along with a strong and coherent economy unlike the rest of the countries.

00:07:50.840 --> 00:07:55.640
The US thus insisted that the gold along with the American dollar must be the centerpiece of the Bretton Woods system that

00:07:55.640 --> 00:08:00.600
was agreed upon according to the United Nations Monetary and Financial Conference or the Bretton Woods

00:08:00.600 --> 00:08:05.080
Conference at the time. An ounce of gold has been determined ever since to be equal to $35.

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:10.480
Accordingly, most countries of the world have fixed the values ​​of their currencies on the US dollar as the United States was

00:08:10.480 --> 00:08:15.080
guaranteeing all countries the convertibility of the dollar into gold and vice versa.

00:08:15.080 --> 00:08:21.760
However, due to the US involvement in Vietnam, the increase in public debt, the negative balance of payments

00:08:21.760 --> 00:08:29.120
and the intensive US printing of dollars to pay government expenditures on military and social programs;

00:08:29.120 --> 00:08:36.400
many countries began to worry as the dollar may lose its value, so they began exchanging it from the United States for gold.

00:08:36.400 --> 00:08:45.920
As a result, US President Richard Nixon issued a package of economic measures in 1971,wherein he feared that gold would run out of the United States, 

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:50.560
on top of these measures, ending the convertibility of the dollar to gold unilaterally without consulting any country,

00:09:05.680 --> 00:09:10.040
As for buying gold in rubles, Russia must abide by the same rules,

00:09:10.040 --> 00:09:13.760
which is the convertibility of rubles into gold and here is the problem.

00:09:13.760 --> 00:09:18.920
Russia may find itself in a similar situation to that of the United States in 1971.

00:09:18.920 --> 00:09:25.440
If investors or the public lose confidence in the ruble for any reason, there will be a bank run to the Russian Central Bank

00:09:25.440 --> 00:09:29.560
to withdraw the gold and replace it with the ruble. This as a result

00:09:29.560 --> 00:09:32.600
would lead to serious problems in Russia such as economic instability.

00:09:32.600 --> 00:09:37.360
As we know, after the imposition of Western sanctions on Russia, which caused the worst

00:09:37.360 --> 00:09:42.480
economic crisis for the country since the fall of the Soviet Union in 1991,

00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:46.760
families began to get rid of the collapsed ruble and buy gold instead.

00:09:46.760 --> 00:09:51.240
Therefore, the Russian Central Bank stopped buying gold in mid-March

00:09:51.240 --> 00:09:59.000
in order to give people the opportunity without crowding out. This was also a smart move by the Russian Central at the time.

00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:03.680
That is why it has set a specific time period for buying gold in rubles, as we previously  said.

00:10:03.680 --> 00:10:08.480
Gold for Russia is the type of assets that it can sell to support the ruble.

00:10:08.480 --> 00:10:12.880
It is one of the main assets that the Russian Central Bank can resort to

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:16.280
to ease the crisis and absorb the effects of Western sanctions,

00:10:16.280 --> 00:10:21.120
therefore it is an important and decisive weapon in the confrontation with the West in general.

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:27.960
Since 2014, as the United States and Europe imposed sanctions on Russia in response to the annexation of Crimea,

00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:34.000
Russia began to make its economy more resilient in the face of sanctions and strengthen its defenses against

00:10:34.000 --> 00:10:41.200
 economic restrictions through hoarding gold and foreign exchange reserves and diversifying away from the dollar.

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:44.480
For this reason, we note that Russia's gold holdings have tripled

00:10:44.480 --> 00:10:49.560
than they were during its annexation of the Crimea 8 years ago.

00:10:49.560 --> 00:10:57.440
In numbers, in March 2014, gold accounted for 8.9% of Russia's total foreign exchange reserves.

00:10:57.440 --> 00:11:01.800
In the last published data of Russian reserves on the website of the Central Bank of Russia

00:11:01.800 --> 00:11:07.760
on January 31, 2022, the proportion of gold constitutes 20.9%.

00:11:07.760 --> 00:11:12.480
How much gold does Russia currently have? Russia has the fifth

00:11:12.480 --> 00:11:15.800
largest deposit of gold in the world. A senior White House

00:11:15.800 --> 00:11:19.480
official said that before Russia invaded Ukraine, it had about

00:11:19.480 --> 00:11:24.520
$140 billion US $ in gold, in other words; about 2,300 tons of gold

00:11:24.520 --> 00:11:27.560
are currently in the possession of the Russian Central Bank.

00:11:27.560 --> 00:11:29.880
This is in addition to the annual production that will join this

00:11:29.880 --> 00:11:34.080
amount to reach 330 tons of gold by the end of the current year.

00:11:34.080 --> 00:11:37.920
That amount alone is equivalent to about $20 billion today.

00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:41.560
Of course, the sanctions imposed on Russia isolated it from

00:11:41.560 --> 00:11:46.120
major parts of the global financial markets and froze nearly half

00:11:46.120 --> 00:11:49.480
of its foreign exchange reserves, equivalent to $300 billion,

00:11:49.480 --> 00:11:54.640
specifically foreign currencies such as dollars and euros that were in Western banks.

00:11:54.640 --> 00:11:58.280
However, the 2,300 tons of gold were originally in Russia

00:11:58.280 --> 00:12:01.680
therefore Western countries could not control or freeze them.

00:12:01.680 --> 00:12:06.000
That is why this stock of gold is what is left over from foreign reserves,

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:11.400
in addition to about $100 billion US dollars between Russia and China.

00:12:11.400 --> 00:12:16.440
That’s why gold is of value for Russia, yet, in order to be able to benefit from this treasure,

00:12:16.440 --> 00:12:22.040
it has to move it beyond its borders in order to sell it. That is why

00:12:22.040 --> 00:12:29.040
the United States, Europe and their allies moved quickly to block this hole, targeting Russia's giant gold stockpile.

00:12:29.040 --> 00:12:34.600
On March 24, the United States announced, along with the Group of Seven industrialized countries

00:12:34.600 --> 00:12:40.560
(which includes other than the United States: Canada, France, Germany, Italy, Japan

00:12:40.560 --> 00:12:47.280
and the United Kingdom, in addition to the European Union allies) to ban dealing with Russian gold.

00:12:47.280 --> 00:12:53.560
The US Treasury, for example, has issued a directive stating that any gold-related transaction

00:12:53.560 --> 00:12:57.360
of the Russian Central Bank is covered by existing sanctions.

00:12:57.360 --> 00:13:02.320
This was the first ban on trade with Russia linked to the gold markets.

00:13:02.320 --> 00:13:10.120
On the same day of the ban, British Prime Minister Boris Johnson said there were indications that Russia was using its

00:13:10.120 --> 00:13:19.040
gold to evade sanctions, and that Britain would take steps to ensure Russia could not sell bullion. The ban on Russian gold,

00:13:19.040 --> 00:13:24.120
of course, was preceded by sanctions and restrictions on Russian gold companies by Western stock exchanges.

00:13:24.120 --> 00:13:32.600
For example, on March 7, the London Bullion Market Association, or LBMA for short, suspended six Russian

00:13:32.600 --> 00:13:39.320
refineries for refining precious metals, which means that they will not be able to sell either gold or silver in the London market,

00:13:39.320 --> 00:13:48.960
which is the largest gold market in the world. Few hours later, CME Group, which runs the largest US gold exchange,

00:13:48.960 --> 00:13:53.280
the Chicago Mercantile Exchange, also suspended six Russian Dahab refineries.

00:13:53.280 --> 00:14:01.320
Therefore, the sanctions imposed on Russian gold prevent individuals, including gold dealers, distributors, wholesalers,

00:14:01.320 --> 00:14:09.240
buyers, and financial institutions, from buying, selling, or facilitating transactions related to Russian gold,

00:14:09.240 --> 00:14:12.880
whether from the Russian Central Bank or Russian companies themselves.

00:14:12.880 --> 00:14:21.560
This ban is not limited to Western countries, it threatens any entity in any country (has the intention to deal in Russian gold)

00:14:21.560 --> 00:14:27.360
with secondary sanctions even if it is in a major country allied with Russia like China.

00:14:27.360 --> 00:14:31.960
So, does this mean that this 2,300 tons of gold has no advantage?

00:14:31.960 --> 00:14:35.920
Will Russia be not able to deal with any part of it or sell it outside its borders?

00:14:35.920 --> 00:14:43.360
In theory, yes, it has no value according to the current situation, however in practice and on the ground, Russia can use complex,

00:14:43.360 --> 00:14:47.600
dangerous and difficult-to-track schemes to truck gold abroad away

00:14:47.600 --> 00:14:51.320
from the United States and Western countries. Nevertheless,

